From: silentsudin <25103587+silentsudin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:24:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] anv: no CM retry check outside Wine processes

anv_cm_retry_failed() runs at every vkCreateDevice. With the patched
driver installed system-wide, programs that are neither Wine processes
nor given ANV_CM_SPV_DIR (the compositor, desktop apps) would each log
"ANV CM: neither ANV_CM_SPV_DIR nor WINEPREFIX is set". Return early
for them; Wine processes behave as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/intel/vulkan/anv_shader_compile.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/intel/vulkan/anv_shader_compile.c b/src/intel/vulkan/anv_shader_compile.c
index 1595a19..dd82e4d 100644
--- a/src/intel/vulkan/anv_shader_compile.c
+++ b/src/intel/vulkan/anv_shader_compile.c
@@ -1425,6 +1425,10 @@ void
 anv_cm_retry_failed(struct anv_device *device)
 {
    char sdir[512], mark[600];
+   /* Not a Wine process and no shim folder given: nothing to retry. Return before anv_cm_spv_dir(), which would print
+    * its warning for every Vulkan program on a system-wide install (compositor, desktop). */
+   if (!getenv("ANV_CM_SPV_DIR") && !getenv("WINEPREFIX"))
+      return;
    if (!anv_cm_spv_dir(sdir, sizeof(sdir)))
       return;
    snprintf(mark, sizeof(mark), "%s/compile_failed.txt", sdir);
